      en: "The Bosai Minerals Plant in Linden, Guyana, is a bauxite processing facility that has been operational since the 1960s. Acquired by Chinese investors in the early 2000s, it underwent significant upgrades to increase efficiency. The plant produces calcined bauxite and alumina, primarily for export. It employs around 800 workers and has an annual output of approximately 1.5 million tons. The facility is located on the Demerara River, facilitating barge transport. It contributes roughly half of Guyana's bauxite production and is a key economic driver for the town of Linden.",
