      en: "The Port of New Amsterdam is a major river port on the Berbice River in northeastern Guyana. It handles over 2 million tons of cargo annually, primarily agricultural produce like rice, as well as timber and bauxite. The port has multiple berths and storage facilities, and underwent dredging to accommodate larger vessels. It is operated by the Guyana National Shipping Corporation and is a key economic asset for the Berbice region. Expansion projects aim to develop deep-water capabilities.",
